From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] kleaf: ddk_config: don't source a Kconfig Kconfig.ext already sources

kleaf's DDK config step (create_kconfig_ext_step.bzl) copies the inherited
Kconfig.ext and appends a `source` line for every Kconfig of the DDK
module's dependency set. The gs201 Kconfig.ext.gs201 already sources
touch/common and radio/samsung/s5300, which touch/fingerprint DDK modules
also declare as their kconfig, so they end up sourced twice. 6.18's
kconfig tolerated that; since 6.19 it is an error ("repeated inclusion of
..."), and every such module's ddk_config fails. Skip a Kconfig whose path
the file already sources.

lynx-mainline describes this fix but never committed it: .gitignore's
unanchored `build/` also matched kernel/patches-lynx/build/.
---
diff --git a/kleaf/impl/ddk/ddk_config/create_kconfig_ext_step.bzl b/kleaf/impl/ddk/ddk_config/create_kconfig_ext_step.bzl
index f808a6f..12ee8b1 100644
--- a/kleaf/impl/ddk/ddk_config/create_kconfig_ext_step.bzl
+++ b/kleaf/impl/ddk/ddk_config/create_kconfig_ext_step.bzl
@@ -97,6 +97,14 @@ def _create_kconfig_ext_step_compare_in_analysis_phase_impl(
             KCONFIG_EXT_PREFIX=$(realpath ${kconfig_ext_dir} --relative-to ${ROOT_DIR}/${KERNEL_DIR})/
             (
                 for kconfig in $(cat ${combined_kconfig_depset_file}); do
+                    # junkyard: skip a Kconfig the inherited Kconfig.ext already
+                    # sources. Kconfig rejects a repeated `source` since 6.19
+                    # ("repeated inclusion of ..."), and the gs201 Kconfig.ext
+                    # sources touch/common and radio/s5300, which DDK modules
+                    # also declare as their kconfig.
+                    if grep -qF "${kconfig}\\"" ${kconfig_ext_dir}/Kconfig.ext; then
+                        continue
+                    fi
                     mod_kconfig_rel=$(realpath ${ROOT_DIR} --relative-to ${ROOT_DIR}/${KERNEL_DIR})/${kconfig}
                     echo 'source "'"${mod_kconfig_rel}"'"' >> ${kconfig_ext_dir}/Kconfig.ext
                 done
